      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s existence is closely tied to the opening of the Cairo and Vincennes Railroad on December 9 1872.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Crossville was incorporated on September 30 1895, with its charter filed the next day at 11:05 am.",
